## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)

- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with
  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as
  completed with no evidence attached.
- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into
  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly
  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.
- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: "I will attach it when
  the run finishes" is unfulfillable by construction.

Run `task-board spawn directives "$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID"` at safe checkpoints,
at most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.
Directives have no delivery timer.
Save before cancel; pause/reroute safely.
